      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here, and in all other places where you pass forward the r-value parameter, you want to use `std::forward\u003cTYPE\u003e` to ensure it doesn\u0027t turn into an l-value, and end up copying the function. So for instance, here you\u0027d do:\n\n```\n    CheckIOAttributes(func, func-\u003eReturnAttributes(), func-\u003eReturnType(), std::forward\u003cIS_NOT_STRUCT\u003e(is_not_struct_impl),\n                      std::forward\u003cIS_STRUCT\u003e(is_struct_impl));\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 74,
